He and others have been talking about "people who want the game harder",
and I suppose most people don't want it harder.  On my part I find the
game very well balanced and the wand of wishing not very relevant in
this "NH-universe of many different tactics, strategies, and randomness".
The wand is powerful but novices can usually not make optimal, sometimes
make even bad choices for their wishes, and nevertheless lose such a
game.  For the experienced, who can enter the castle and pass through
Gehennom, the wand is not very relevant.  And for medium advanced, who
manage to get until the entrance of the castle but not yet in?  Maybe
they gain the most from that wand, but mainly if they got it *early* - and
in this rare case just for that single game.  If the mid-range players
can enter and survive the castle, they fall into the skill category where
the wand becomes more and more irrelevant.  You *can* draw the conclusion
that the wand charges should be reduced; but there's really no need any
more *at* the castle level and still less(*) need before the castle level,
IMO.

(*) "less than no need" - well, you know what I mean...

